@format 1
@id queue.clear-tabs
@title Clear all tab contents
@area 4. Queue and scheduling
@entry input
@summary Confirm the command, then use each workspace's activation-independent media reset to clear preview, flow, files, and group state.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@related files.clear, preview.close-media, split.section-delete

@alias console = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PConsole
@alias tabset = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.LTabset
@alias workspace = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.PWorkspace
@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer
@alias list = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PList
@alias group = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PGroup
@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow

[input] Clear Tabs requested <input>
- Receive the Clear Tabs command @ console.PConsoleTabsHandle(...)
> confirm

[confirm] Confirm removal <decision>
- Apply the destructive-action confirmation preference @ console.PConsoleDestructiveConfirm(...)
? "Clearing is declined" > unchanged
? "Clearing proceeds" > clear

[clear] Clear each workspace <process>
- Iterate every tab and invoke its tab-owned media reset @ tabset.LTabsetContentClear(...)
- Force-close loaded viewer media even when the workspace is inactive @ workspace.PWorkspaceMediaClear(...)
@ viewer.PViewerMediaClose(...)
- Clear flow source, spool, cursor, sections, keyframes, waveform, and selection without an active-command guard @ workspace.PWorkspaceMediaClear(...)
@ flow.PFlowClear(...)
- Clear a non-empty file list and publish its removed paths @ workspace.PWorkspaceMediaClear(...)
@ list.PListClear(...)
- Clear merge-group state @ workspace.PWorkspaceMediaClear(...)
@ group.PGroupClear(...)
> complete

[complete] Tab clearing finishes <output>
= Viewer, player, flow, sections, keyframes, waveform, file-list, selection, and group state are cleared in active and inactive tabs.

[unchanged] Tabs unchanged <output>
= No tab content is cleared.
